There are crucial differences between what happened in the novel and the donghua. In the novel, Liu Mei and Wang Lin had sex under the influence of the Thousand Illusions Lust Domain (cf. note of episode 99). Liu Mei cultivates a resentful spirit inside her body for 100 years and then gives birth to it.\NThis subplot was obviously censored in the donghua which took the route of having Liu Mei steal a part of Wang Lin's soul to make a resentful spirit out of it. The outcome is the same.\N---\NWang Lin’s face was filled with ferocity as he shouted at Liu Mei, “What's inside it ?!”\N\NLiu Mei revealed a smile, but her eyes were filled with pain. She then looked at Wang Lin with a wider smile. “You don’t recognize it? No, with your cultivation, you should be able to recognize it.”\N\N“There is a legend among mortals. If a person loses several children, the souls of those children will not dissipate, they will always follow you and watch you. They will seem to be saying something, but you won’t be able to hear. It won’t be until the moment of your death that you finally hear them ask ‘Daddy, why don’t you want me…’”\N\NLiu Mei’s voice was a bit strange; there was even a trace of madness within it.\N\N“I refined this child inside my body for a century until he finally became a resentful spirit. When he gained consciousness, I kept telling him that it was his father who abandoned him. His father is called Wang Lin!”

